weigh the fewer shortfalls. That gives ≈ −5970 to −6170.\n\n**Product 1:**\n- Candidate 0 orders about 0.9 of the forecast (583). About 98 units missed, ≈ −6920.\n- Candidate 7 (619) ≈ −6820, candidate 2 (657) ≈ −6800, candidate 3 ≈ −6830, candidate 5 (679) ≈ −6930.\n\n**Totals for the daily plans:** candidate 7 ≈ −12520, candidate 0 ≈ −12650, candidate 2 ≈ −12770, candidate 3 ≈ −12820, candidate 5 ≈ −13100. Candidate 1 orders about 1.2–1.25 of the forecast, so it overstocks even more and does worse still.\n\n**Batch plans:**\n- Candidate 4 (every 3 days) saves 360 in fees. But it carries about one extra day of demand in stock on average, which costs about 790 in holding. On top of that, each delivery of about 150 units risks hitting the 188-unit capacity.\n- Candidate 6 (every 2 days) saves 260 but pays about 395 more in holding.\n- Both end up below candidate 7.\n\n**Robustness:** candidate 7 orders slightly above expected demand for product 0 and slightly below for product 1. If actual demand drifts either way, the swing in its result is moderate. It doesn't pile up stock the way candidates 2, 3 and 5 do, and it isn't chronically short like candidate 0.\n\nThese numbers are approximate mental estimates, not a simulation. The gap between candidates 7 and 0 (about 130) is within the error of the estimate. The gap to the rest is larger."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:08:49.011Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQansi1MvAbaCTnk19U6"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}